---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  Put the code in a <code>&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;</code> inside the element, or set the
  <code>value</code> property. Indentation shared by every line is removed, and JavaScript, HTML
  and CSS are formatted unless you set <code>format="false"</code>. Syntax colors come from the
  theme's color roles, so they follow light, dark and custom themes.
</p>
<p>
  Without a title, the copy button floats at the top end. It appears when you hover over the block
  or move keyboard focus into it, and it is always visible on touch screens.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-code-highlighter style='width: 100%;' language='javascript' is:raw>
    <pre><code>
      const greet = (name) => `Hello, ${name}!`;
      export { greet };
    </code></pre>
  </wc-code-highlighter>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3 class='text-title-medium'>Setting the value</h3>
<p>
  The <code>value</code> property takes the code as written. Entities are not decoded there, so
  set it from script.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-code-highlighter style='width: 100%;' id='code-highlighter-value' language='css'></wc-code-highlighter>

  <script is:inline>
    document.getElementById('code-highlighter-value').value =
      ':root { --color-primary: #0b57d0; } .card > h2 { margin: 0; }';
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>
